    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1725">

                <pb facs="1102" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11D29/52.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Answering your telegram April 7. Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs to-day
                    states that he will have conference with Secretary of Government and Justice,
                    judge, and attorney of the Supreme <pb facs="1103" n="987" xml:id="pg987"/>
                    Court, without further delay, for the purpose of hastening proceedings. He
                    promised to do this last Tuesday. He adds assurance of strict justice being
                    decreed in accordance with law and the practice of civilization.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
